NNAAMMEE
     ggssttaatt — print statistics about GEOM disks

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ggssttaatt [--aabbBBccCCddooppss] [--ff _f_i_l_t_e_r] [--II _i_n_t_e_r_v_a_l]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggssttaatt utility can be used to monitor I/O transactions of geom(4) de‐
     vices.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa      Only display providers that are at least 0.1% busy.

     --bb      Batch mode.  Collect numbers, print and exit.  Default if stdout
             is not a tty.

     --BB      Endless batch mode.  Same as batch mode, but does not exit after
             collecting the first set of data.

     --cc      Enable display of geom(4) consumers too.  The default is to show
             statistics only for geom(4) producers.

     --CC      CSV output mode.  Implies endless batch mode, but output is in
             the form of comma-separated values, with ISO 8601-like time‐
             stamps.

     --dd      Enable display of statistics for delete (BIO_DELETE) operations.

     --ff _f_i_l_t_e_r
             A regular expression that can be used to only show statistics for
             some devices.  Only devices with the names matching _f_i_l_t_e_r will
             be displayed.  The format of the regular expression is described
             in re_format(7).

     --II _i_n_t_e_r_v_a_l
             Refresh the ggssttaatt display every _i_n_t_e_r_v_a_l microseconds.  Adding a
             suffix of ss, mmss, or uuss (the default) indicates that the update
             interval is specified in seconds, milliseconds, or microseconds,
             respectively.

     --oo      Enable display of statistics for other operations (BIO_FLUSH).

     --pp      Only display physical providers (those with rank of 1).

     --ss      Enable blocks' size statistics.

IINNTTEERRAACCTTIIVVEE CCOOMMMMAANNDDSS
     These commands are currently recognized if ggssttaatt is not running in batch
     mode:

     <<       Halve the update interval.

     >>       Double the update interval.

     cc       Toggle display of geom(4) consumers.

     ff       Display only devices with the names matching regular expression
             filter (prompt for filter).

     FF       Remove device filter.

     qq       Quit ggssttaatt.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ggssttaatt utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     systat(1), geom(4), iostat(8), vmstat(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
